course: dictionary
lesson: 9190
title: What does society mean?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Society has three main meanings. First, it means all the people living together in a country or the world, with their own ways of life, rules and customs. Second, a society is a group or club of people who share an interest or an aim. Third, society can mean company, being with other people.
explain: Read the words around it to choose the right meaning. «London Zoo opened in 1828 as a zoo for science, set up by the Zoological Society of London.» Here a society is a group of people working together for a shared aim, not all the people in a country.
explain: Phrases help too. «Modern society» means the people and way of life of today, and «a member of society» means one person who belongs to the community. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Society means all the people living together in a country or the world, with their ways of life, rules and customs.
fact: A society is a group or club of people who share an interest or an aim, like a science society or a drama society.
fact: Society can also mean company, being with other people.
fact: «Animal welfare society» is one example: a group of people working together to look after animals.
fact: «Quakers, the Religious Society of Friends, worship mostly in silence» shows that a society can be a religious group too.
exercise: «The Apostrophe Protection Society was set up in 2001.» In this sentence, what is a society? | All the people living in a country | Being with other people | A kind of game | *A group of people who share an aim
exercise: In the phrase «modern society», what does society mean? | A kind of ice on ponds | Being quiet | A club for drawing | *The people living together today, with their rules and customs
exercise: Which is the best example of a society? | A stone in a pond | A single bird sitting on a tree | *A science society, a group of people who share an interest | A puzzle book
test: «The Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents» gives advice about ice on ponds and lakes. In this name, what does society mean? | A kind of sport | Being with other people | *A group or organisation of people with a shared aim | Everyone living in the country
test: Mrs Bell says, «I enjoy society at the club, with friends all around me.» What does society mean here? | A tall tree | *Company, being with other people | A ship at sea | Rules and laws for everyone
exam: «Quakers, the Religious Society of Friends, worship mostly in silence and are known for peace-making.» Which meaning of society fits best? | *A group of people who share a belief and an aim | Being with other people | A game of cards | All the people in the world
